46, "color": "W", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -12.22, "lead_after": -12.0, "points_lost": 0.22, "best": "pass"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Chasing stones on the left while the lead drained", "summary": "White won by 12 points (W+12) after two passes. The game was level at the start, but GPT-6.1 Sol lost 7.3 points per move and made 8 blunders. The 20k blundered 7 times as well and kept handing back the big swings. GPT-6.1 Sol's moves 11 and 13 put Black well behind, and the 20k's gifts never let it catch up.", "moments": [{"turn": 11, "text": "F5 is where the game tilts. It lost 9.7 points, taking Black from -1.7 to -11.4, and the engine preferred D5. Black's stones along the fifth row became a wall pressed against White's fourth-row stones rather than a claim on the centre."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "C6 lost 17.3 points, sinking Black from -16.3 to -33.6, and the engine wanted H4 on the right. White's reply C5 lost 16.6 right back (-17.0). B6 and A6 later cost 22.1 and 23.0, the left-side stones were all gone from the final board, and White captured 5 stones in total."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "The 20k's E3 lost 24.0 points, moving the lead from -40.1 to -16.1. The 20k had been handed a huge lead and gave much of it straight back, which is why this game stayed close to a coin flip in the middle."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "F2 was Black's worst move: 27.1 points, dropping the lead from -16.1 to -43.2. The engine's choice was H4. The two Black stones at F3 and G3 sat under White's fourth-row line and the new White stone at E3, and F2 did nothing to ease that."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "H4 was finally the engine's own first choice, and it lost only 0.3 points. It came too late to change the result, but from here the lead held between -10.5 and -19.7 until the two passes."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran works on the current position or on records: current-position-liberties.js (inspectLiberties) counts chain